OL,3,GNEWSAAuthors warn libraries proposals
OL,4,Acould 'pave the way' for censorship
OL,5,
OL,6,FMore than 160 writers and illustrators
OL,7,Fhave signed an open letter raising
OL,8,Fconcerns about plans for Northern
OL,9,FIreland's public libraries.
OL,11,FThe signatories, who include Oliver
OL,12,FJeffers, Jan Carson, Wendy Erskine and
OL,13,FLucy Caldwell, said they were concerned
OL,14,Fthe proposals "could pave the way for
OL,15,Fbook bans, restrictions for minority
OL,16,Fgroup visibility and library closures".
OL,18,FCommunities Minister Gordon Lyons said
OL,19,Flibrarians would decide which books to
OL,20,Fstock and that he wanted libraries to
OL,21,Fremain "open to all on the same basis".
OL,23,APub: 24-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
